--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 -- CONFIGURE THE IPv6 CLIENT: ONE REACHABLE SERVER, ONE UNREACHABLE  PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Method: configure both IPv6 servers in one go, on purpose. The exchange under test and
the control that must NOT match are then in the same capture, at the same moment, through
the same interface, so nothing about the two differs except the address.

  reachable : fd32:b1f0:dff8:1603::1   -- tb277's own ntpd, on eth3. MUST be used.
  control   : fd32:b1f0:dff8:1603::99  -- an unused address on the same /64. Nothing is
                                          there. MUST NOT be used, and must draw no reply.

The CLI surface was read read-only first (never `<cmd>` + CR):
awplus(config)#ntp server ?
  A.B.C.D   IPv4 address of NTP Server
  WORD      FQDN of NTP Server
  X:X::X:X  IPv6 address of NTP Server
                                           <-- an IPv6 server literal IS accepted by the
                                               parser; there is no separate IPv6 command

The capture was started FIRST, in the background, and only then was the DUT configured --
two calls issued in one block run one after the other, so a watcher started "beside" a
change sees nothing of it (memory two-console-calls-in-one-block-run-sequentially):

