STEP 5 -- THE REMOVAL LIMB: SILENCE ON THE WIRE, WITH THE LEG STILL UP      PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Method: remove BOTH `ntp server` lines, then prove on the wire that the DUT stops
completely. A silent capture only means something if the leg is demonstrably alive at the
same time, so the leg is pinged inside the capture window, not before it or after it.
The capture was started FIRST and the removal applied into it.

tb277$ tools/tb capture tb277 ntp61022 eth3 170 t44299-s5-removed.pcap udp port 123
   (started 12:26:06 local; removal applied at box UTC 23:26:11)

awplus#configure terminal
awplus(config)#no ntp server fd32:b1f0:dff8:1603::1
awplus(config)#no ntp server fd32:b1f0:dff8:1603::99
awplus(config)#end
awplus#show running-config | include ntp
                                           <-- NOTHING: both lines gone
awplus#show ntp status
                                           <-- COMPLETELY EMPTY again
awplus#show ntp associations
                                           <-- COMPLETELY EMPTY again
awplus#show ntp counters
                                           <-- COMPLETELY EMPTY again

  The three NTP show commands have returned EXACTLY to the state recorded in the setup
  reads before step 1. That round trip is what makes the empty read meaningful: empty ->
  populated -> empty, driven only by configuration. It also re-confirms
  platforms/x960.md §7H.5 in both directions on this build.
  The removal is proved by RE-READING the configuration, never by the absence of an error.

INSIDE THE SAME WINDOW, the leg was pinged to prove it was still up:
