                                           <-- ntpwire exit 2, the control exit code
   (writer confirmed exited at 12:28:56 before the file was read)

  => STEP 5 PASS: 170 s of capture, ZERO NTP packets. The DUT's poll interval immediately
     before the removal was 64 s, so this window covers about 2.6 polls that would have
     happened and did not. The leg carried 4/4 ICMPv6 at 0.5 ms in the middle of that same
     window, so the silence is the DUT's, not a dead link. The client stops completely
     when the configuration is removed; there is no leftover polling.
     (This capture's filter was `udp port 123` alone, which is why the frame count is 0
     rather than "some ICMPv6 and no NTP". The independent liveness evidence is the ping,
