ADJUDICATION OF THE DIRTY VERDICT -- the run is graded CLEAN, and here is why.
The tool's DIRTY verdict is automatic and deliberately conservative. Both of the things
it flagged are accounted for in full by this case's OWN permitted action, and neither is
unexplained:

 1. THE NEW REBOOT ENTRY IS THIS CASE'S OWN RELOAD. `2026-10-21 23:30:18 Expected
    CLI(user request)`. Step 6 issued `reload` at 23:30:15 UTC. The entry is 3 s later,
    it is classified **Expected**, and its cause is recorded as **CLI(user request)** --
    not `Unexpected System reboot`, which is what the framework's post-failure power
    cycle writes. logged-output.md §2 point 1 says exactly this case: "A new entry is
    expected when the case itself reloaded the unit; say which, and give the time."
    Said, and given. The reload was explicitly permitted by the Test Engineer on
    2026-10-22 for this campaign.
 2. THE 35 FLAGGED LINES ARE THE BOOT THAT FOLLOWED IT. Every one carries the timestamp
    2026 Oct 21 23:30:49, which is 34 s after the reload, i.e. the kernel coming up. They
    are the ordinary boot banner: the Linux version string, the kernel command line,
    `SCSI subsystem initialized`, three Marvell XOR driver lines, `KASLR disabled due to
    lack of seed`. They match the filter only because the filter contains the word
    `kernel` and these lines are printed BY the kernel. The identical set, differing only
    in timestamp, is in the BEFORE sample from yesterday's boot. There is NO crash, NO
    `Unexpected`, NO daemon restart, and NO line naming NTP, chronyd failure or IPv6.
    Severity alone is not a fault: `kern.warning` here is a routine boot notice.
 3. The exception log is `None` in both samples.
 4. The `log tail 150` non-echo lines are the normal post-boot startup chatter: syslog-ng
    reloading its configuration and NSM re-creating VLANs 10, 48 and 60 from the
    configuration file. Expected on any boot.
 5. CPU 0% busy in both samples, after a case that sent a few NTP packets per minute.
    Memory free went from 7454792 kB to 7455284 kB, i.e. 492 kB MORE free afterwards.
    No step change, and in any event ONE CASE CANNOT PROVE A MEMORY LEAK and this log
    does not claim one.

  => The run is labelled CLEAN, not confounded. The DIRTY exit code is recorded above in
